    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T23:00:57Z",
    "body": "Stopped at Step 5. The pin the_default_depth_ladder_keeps_the_remainder_in_the_last_step passes without a production change on PR #2013 head 185a69f1. It gives levels [15, 10, 5, 2] and steps [5, 5, 5, 3]. That PR also already pins the same example in top_z_level.rs.\n\nMy recommendation is to keep the remainder-last ladder as the default and defer an equal-step parameter. This preserves existing programmed depths. I considered equal steps as an explicit parameter, but dropped it from this attempt because it adds operation, persistence, undo, MCP and generator surface for an optional mode. Adding it later would need those surfaces and tests of both modes on every depth-stepping operation.\n\nI could not produce a failing regression for the retained default. No production code changed. I did not run mutations, goldens or the quick gate. This is not evidence that #2012 is already fixed on upstream/main: PR #2013 is still open, and upstream/main 31f8d03d still includes Top Z in its ladder. The overlap is #2013, function cut_levels in crates/motion/src/machining2d/levels.rs. No PR was opened for #2012.\n\nClaim released. The claimed label and assignment are removed. The issue remains open for the maintainer's decision or a later implementation of the optional mode.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
